<h1>Dennis &quot;DJ&quot; Doran</h1>
<p>44th Ward alderman, on the Chicago ballot February 23, 2027.</p>
<p><a href="https://www.djdoran.com/" rel="nofollow noopener">Campaign site (djdoran.com)</a></p>
<h2>Running on</h2>
<p>Announced in May 2026 a run for the seat held by Ald. Bennett Lawson. His campaign lists public safety, including fewer thefts and faster police response; development that favors local small businesses over national chains on corridors like Broadway and Belmont; and transit fixes including cleaner CTA stations, more bike lanes, and more reliable service.</p>
<h2>Background</h2>
<p>Owner of Aequalitas Media, an LGBTQ+-focused media company; Air Force veteran and pilot; former executive director of the nonprofit Chicago Deserves Better, which works toward a Chicago city charter. Ran for mayor in 2023.</p>
